<title>UK: BP/Mobil Coryton to close crude unit for eight day.</title>
<headline>BP/Mobil Coryton to close crude unit for eight day.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A crude distillation unit at the Coryton refinery jointly operated by British Petroleum Plc and Mobil Corp is to be shut down for planned maintenance at the weekend, a press spokesman for the companies said.</p>
<p>&quot;The unit will close in three days time for planned repairs to a heater unit which will take about 8-10 days,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said the repairs at the refinery, which processes 178,000 barrels per day, were part of a planned maintenance schedule and the company had sufficient stocks to meet requirements over the period.</p>
<p>--Colin Wooster, London newsroom, +44 171 542 7456</p>
